  "auditor_patch": {
    "why": "issue #71 \u00a71 -- prevent the fail-open from recurring and let the shared gate prove completion. Tightly scoped: (a) both shared gate modules stopped defaulting a missing train_end epoch to 3000 and now require an explicit epoch, a linked ckpt_saved record, a readable checkpoint whose own metadata says 3000, and a matching declared checkpoint path; (b) every R4/R5 trainer now logs epoch=EPOCHS plus output_json_sha256 in its train_end event.",
    "what_was_not_touched": "no learned weights, no historical SIDs, no train/valid/test splits, no ER threshold, no historical gate.json or stage2_metrics.json, no Stage3 result, and no Stage2/Stage3 rerun. Historical training JSONL files are byte-unchanged.",
    "historical_gates_left_as_they_are": true
  },
